content.text:
At 320 things still fit but:
- Top brand sub wraps ("IDLE MINING CO." wraps) and "GAME SAVED" wraps; some visual awkwardness, not breaking.
- Stats labels wrap ("LIFETIME HAUL" two lines, "ores brought up" two lines). Acceptable.
- Eyebrow ellipsized "CURRENT CLAIM · OLD IR..." good.
- The mine button and sell button fit.
- Footer not visible until scroll.
- The prompt is very long but fits exactly width 281? It touches edges: pill spans x=22..? Actually prompt width ~250 and panel 281. Fine.
- The scene composition at 320: ore and crystal overlap miner? The crystal at right 16% looks close to pickaxe. Fine.

Could improve top bar at 320: hide brand-sub maybe, hide save pill text to just dot, but not necessary. Maybe better responsive: at max-width 360, brand-sub display none, save-pill padding smaller. Also stats: reduce label font to 7px? Hmm.

To support small phones well, add media max-width 360:
.brand-sub{display:none}
.topbar{gap:6px}
.save-pill{font-size:9px;padding:6px 8px}
.stats-row{gap:5px}
.stat-card{padding:9px 8px}
.stat-label{font-size:7px}
.stat-value{font-size:17px}
.stat-extra{font-size:8px}
.mine-btn{font-size:10px;padding:11px 8px}
.sell-btn{font-size:9px;padding:11px 7px}
.power-note{font-size:9px}
.mine-header{left:12px;right:12px}
.eyebrow{font-size:8px}
.depth-badge{font-size:8px;padding:5px 7px}
.mine-title{font-size:16px}
.mine-prompt{font-size:9px;padding:5px 8px}
.section-title{font-size:12px}
That will tidy. 320 is rare but good.

Also at 320 "SELL ORE 6 ⛃" is fine; maybe shorten to "SELL 6". Could use CSS hiding "ORE" not easy. Keep.

On the top bar, brand mark + name + save + reset fill width exactly; save pill wrapping "GAME SAVED" into 2 lines is not great. Hide save text at <=360 and show just dot? The save-pill could become a 36px square with dot. But then meaning lost. Alternatively hide the reset button text? It's icon only. The brand-sub wrapping causes height growth. Add nowrap to brand-sub and brand-name. At 320, brand width then ~135; save pill ~90; reset 38; gaps 20 → 283 + padding 24 = 307 fits! Actually the save pill 90 and brand 135 = 225 + reset 38 + gaps 10*2=20 = 283, within 296 content width. But brand-sub text "IDLE MINING CO." wrapped because its container was narrow? brand has gap 12; mark 33; text width = maybe 93; "IDLE MINING CO." at 8px*~0.6=43? It shouldn't wrap. Unless letter-spacing .17em adds ~13 → 56. Fits. The wrap shown "IDLE MINING CO." on two lines ("IDLE MINING" / "CO.") suggests width ~70. Hmm.

At 320, topbar is flex justify-between; brand flex item shrinks because save+reset need space. Save pill is 2 lines due to shrink. So both wrap. Add flex-shrink:0 to save pill and reset; brand text min-width:0. Then topbar might overflow. Better hide save pill text on <=360: keep dot with aria label? Could replace text with "SAVED" via CSS? Use two spans and hide. Simpler add media:
@media(max-width:360px){.save-pill{font-size:0;padding:8px}.save-pill .save-dot{margin:0;width:7px;height:7px}.brand-sub{white-space:nowrap}.day-pill{display:none}}
Brand-sub may still wrap unless nowrap; set white-space:nowrap and brand-name nowrap. Then width check. Brand overall ~33+12+? name 11px "DEEP ROCK" ~65, sub 8px ~66 → brand 111. Save pill dot 23. Reset 38. Gaps 10+10 =20. Total 192 + padding 24 = 216 < 305. Fits easily. Great.

Add small phone CSS.

At 320, the stats labels wrap: with 3 cards each ~90px, "LIFETIME HAUL" 8px * 0.6 *12=58 + letter spacing 12*1.12=13 =71; fits in 90-20=70 → just wraps. Reduce label font to 7px or remove letter-spacing at <=360. Add .stat-label{letter-spacing:.08em} at 360; then fits.

The stat extra "ores brought up" wraps to 2 lines; card height 76 -> may overflow? Screenshot card shows 3 lines but still fits with min-height 76? It shows "ores brought up" two lines and card height ~106 maybe expanded. Grid row auto; okay. Could shorten text "ores mined" via JS? The extra label is static "ores brought up". At 320 we can hide it? Better set .stat-extra{font-size:8px} and allow. Fine.

Let's add the media query. Also maybe at 320 the topbar height 54 with brand 2 lines grows; after nowrap, fine.

Add:
@media(max-width:360px){
.brand-name,.brand-sub{white-space:nowrap}
.brand-sub{font-size:7px;letter-spacing:.12em}
.save-pill{font-size:0;padding:9px 8px}
.save-pill .save-dot{margin:0}
.stat-label{font-size:7px;letter-spacing:.07em}
.stat-value{font-size:17px}
.stat-extra{font-size:8px}
.stat-card{padding:10px 8px;min-height:70px}
.mine-title{font-size:16px}
.eyebrow{font-size:8px;letter-spacing:.11em}
.depth-badge{font-size:8px;padding:6px 8px}
.mine-prompt{font-size:9px;padding:5px 8px}
.mine-btn{font-size:10px;padding:12px 8px}
.sell-btn{font-size:9px;padding:12px 7px}
.power-note{font-size:9px}
.panel{padding:12px}
}

Need base .brand-name/.brand-sub nowrap maybe globally to avoid wrapping at 390? At 390 they didn't wrap. Add nowrap globally to be safe; brand-sub long 15 chars at 10px with spacing ~ maybe 110px, brand total 155; at 320 still fits with dot-only save. So simply add white-space:nowrap globally to .brand-name and .brand-sub. Then at 320 content width 296: brand 33+12+110=155, save dot 23, reset 38, gaps 20 → 236. Fits. Good; no need hide brand-sub. But save pill text "GAME SAVED" at 320 with brand 155 + save 90 + reset 38 + gaps 20 = 303 > 296 → wraps. So hide text at <=360. Good.

Let's add.

